= Presidential Election

The Presidential Election is to be held now

The absence of a candidate for the Polish moderates leaves behind a vacuum, many parties supporting Piłsudski are scrambling to push a candidate to fill the gap left behind by Piłsudski.

- @who

@who
title: Who will be the successor of Piłsudski?

- @witos

@witos
title: Piłsudski proposes Witos as a candidate
face-image: img/portraits/WitosWincenty.jpeg

To ensure that the Sejm and Senat are united against a National Democrats (ChZJN) Presidency, Piłsudski proposes another unity figure for the Polish moderates which is Wincenty Witos, leader of the PSL-P, and Former Prime Minister. but Witos refuses.

@narutowicz
title: Piłsudski proposes Narutowicz as a candidate
face-image: img/Narutowicz_Pilsudski.jpg

To ensure that the Sejm and Senat are united against a National Democrats (ChZJN) Presidency, Piłsudski proposes another unity figure for the Polish moderates which is Gabriel Narutowicz, a non-partisan candidate, closely aligned with Piłsudski, Formed Minister of Public Works and Current Minister of Foreign Affairs.

- @narutoyay
  
@narutoyay
title: Narutowicz Accepts
face-image: img/portraits/NarutowiczGabriel.jpg

With Narutowicz nominated to replace Piłsudski can he expect the Polish Moderates throw their support for him?

For better or worse, Narutowicz candidacy is only supported by the PSL-L and PSL-W.

